Once again, this is very similar to the `Set`'s `.forEach` method.  We start again by creating a new `Map` and adding a few properties to it.  Next we call `.forEach` and pass in a callback to access the key and value of each item in the `Map`.
The callback `function` accepts two parameters, the `value` and the `key` that we have access to.  We can then use the `key` and `value` in the callback to do whatever you need to do with those values.

With that done we have now covered the basic features of `Map`. Now it's time to get out there and start `Map`ping data!

